<Base title="About the tool engineering" description="How the Sense Astro tool starter verifies real browser-only processing, privacy and independent local tests without inventing deployment. " section="About">
 <section class="copy-page"><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT / EVIDENCE</span><h1>Tools that do the work.</h1><p>Sense Tool Atelier is a reference product used to evaluate whether an agent can build a working Astro tool, not just a landing page. Its JSONL Inspector parses actual input, explains failures and creates downloadable output.</p><h2>Testable claims</h2><p>The shipped parser has independent Node tests and the website is exercised through browser test runs after the Astro build. The input is processed locally; the starter includes no backend ingestion endpoint and no analytics or advertising scripts.</p><h2>Boundaries</h2><p>Build success is not public deployment. A canonical containing example.org is reserved documentation, not a live destination. Real hosting and search indexing require authorized owner DNS, TLS and search account evidence.</p><h2>Developer resources</h2><p>Read the repository installation and acceptance instructions, test the declared maximum input and inspect all negative cases before considering external release.</p><p><a class="inline-link" href="/tools/jsonl-inspector/">Use the JSONL inspector</a></p></section>
</Base>
